## Key terms (server configuration — L4)

| Term | Description |
|------|-------------|
| Server roles and services | File server, DNS, DHCP, Active Directory (AD), Hyper-V, and other roles as required by the organisation. Each role has dependencies (e.g. AD requires DNS). The administrator must plan according to organisational requirements, capacity, and compatibility. Installation order and configuration sequence affect stability and security. |
| Storage configuration | RAID levels (e.g. RAID 1, 5, 10) for redundancy and performance; volumes and partitions; quotas for users or shares; backup targets and schedules. Document the storage layout, recovery procedure, and any change history for handover and audit. |
| Security settings | Firewall rules (inbound/outbound), Windows Update or equivalent patch policy, user and group permissions (least privilege), audit policy for login and object access, and encryption (e.g. BitLocker, TLS). All settings must align with organisational security policy and compliance requirements. |
| Configuration documentation | Record of server roles, IP addresses, storage layout, key configuration choices, and change history. Required for handover, troubleshooting, and audit. Format and retention should follow organisational policy. |

